# TRADER — environment contract. Copy to .env and fill in; .env is gitignored and stays so.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ and EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefixes are inlined into client bundles: public, literally.
#
# Three environments, three homes; a value never moves between them through a file.
#   Local       this .env: the compose database and the development sign-in; Clerk's
#               development keys only through `scripts/staging.sh local`, which takes them
#               from .env.staging. Nothing else loads it but the repository's own entry
#               points; no vendor CLI reads it.
#   Staging     the staging Vercel project's variables (the deployment), GitHub's `staging`
#               environment (the deploy job) and a git-ignored .env.staging on this machine.
#               Never written here: tests and the seed refuse to run while DATABASE_URL is set.
#   Production  the production Vercel project's variables and GitHub's `production`
#               environment. The owner's; never in a file on this machine.

# Names stored outside this file, by where each is set. Commented out here: they are never
# put in .env. Each is read where its comment says.
#
# GitHub's `staging` and `production` environments, read by .github/workflows/ci.yml: the
# migrating role's direct connection string (pooling off), Vercel's deploy hook, the
# deployment's address, and Clerk's secret key for the smoke test's sign-in tickets. The
# smoke test's two people are environment variables, not secrets: their sign-in numbers.
# MIGRATOR_URL=
# DEPLOY_HOOK=
# APP_URL=
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
# E2E_ADMIN_PHONE=
# E2E_WORKER_PHONE=
# Expo's token, in both environments, for the phone workflows (preview-phone.yml,
# release-phone.yml), and the store keys in `production` alone, each piped from its download
# into `gh secret set` and deleted in the same step: App Store Connect's key id, issuer and
# .p8, and Google Play's service account.
# EXPO_TOKEN=
# ASC_API_KEY_ID=
# ASC_API_KEY_ISSUER_ID=
# ASC_API_KEY_P8=
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY=
#
# .env.staging, git-ignored on this machine and read only by scripts/staging.sh: the same
# APP_URL, MIGRATOR_URL, CLERK_SECRET_KEY, E2E_ADMIN_PHONE and E2E_WORKER_PHONE as staging's
# GitHub environment, NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (below), and Vercel's protection
# bypass for the staging project, read by apps/web/e2e/staging.spec.ts.
# VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET=
#
# EAS's `preview` and `production` environments, read by apps/mobile/src/config.ts and the
# build: the deployment's address, Clerk's publishable key, the phone's own Sentry project
# (blank, the app reports nothing), and which environment the build is for (also in eas.json's
# profiles). SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN, sensitive, uploads a build's source maps.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TRADER_ENVIRONMENT=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# On this machine only, in Metro's environment for the phone's development sign-in
# (`EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_IDENTITY=enabled pnpm exec expo start`); never in an EAS environment.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_IDENTITY=
# Also in Metro's environment alone: the sync cycle of a development build, in milliseconds,
# 5000 to 60000 (apps/mobile/src/sync/clock.ts). Blank is a minute, and a release build
# always runs a minute.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CYCLE_MS=

# Local Postgres, read by docker-compose.yml through `pnpm db:up`.
# Pick any password; it never leaves this machine.
POSTGRES_USER=trader
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=trader

# Database connection, read by packages/db/src/env.ts (the Drizzle client, drizzle-kit, tests,
# the seed).
# Unset or empty: the three POSTGRES_* variables above reach the compose container on
# 127.0.0.1:5432. Set: used verbatim and the POSTGRES_* variables are not required (Neon).
# Tests and the seed refuse to run while DATABASE_URL is set: they commit fixtures and create
# databases, and belong on the compose server only.
# A deployment's value is the pooled endpoint with trader_app as the login. Migrations and
# onboarding take the direct endpoint as the owner, typed into the owner's shell for that one
# command and never stored here (README.md). While it is set, drizzle-kit refuses
# to run unless TRADER_MIGRATE_PURPOSE in that shell is `deploy` or `owner`, and the
# development identity below is refused.
DATABASE_URL=
# Connections one server instance may hold; blank is 10. The office's server holds at least
# twice the calls one request may batch (apps/web/src/server/db.ts), so a value below that is
# raised to it there. Sized against the database's limit.
DATABASE_POOL_MAX=

# Clerk, the identity provider, read by apps/web/src/server/clerk-env.ts and by Clerk's own
# code. Both keys are needed; with either missing or malformed this server has no Clerk, every
# protected call answers 401 and people.invite invites no one. The publishable key is public,
# the secret key is not. A development instance's keys start pk_test_ / sk_test_.
# The Clerk instance itself must add four claims to its session token (Dashboard, Sessions,
# Customize session token), which apps/web/src/server/clerk-identity.ts reads:
#   {"email":"{{user.primary_email_address}}","email_verified":"{{user.email_verified}}",
#    "phone_number":"{{user.primary_phone_number}}","phone_number_verified":"{{user.phone_number_verified}}"}
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
# The origins a session may have been issued to, comma-separated, each a bare origin
# (scheme, host, port; no path). Blank admits no browser session at all: a token that names
# an origin is refused unless that origin is listed here.
CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES=

# Sentry, the error reporter behind ErrorReporter, read by apps/web/src/server/deploy-env.ts.
# The project's DSN: https, a key, a host and a numeric project. Public by Sentry's own
# definition (it can only submit events). Blank: reports go to stderr alone, as on a
# development machine. Only the minimized event is ever sent (apps/web, sentry-event.ts).
SENTRY_DSN=

# Email, read by apps/web/src/server/mailer.ts: invoices and invitations. Resend's API key
# and the sender, set together or not at all: blank, nothing is emailed and a send answers
# that mail is not configured. The sender is a verified address of the Resend domain, in the
# form `TRADER <address@jpteq.app>`. The key is a secret; it is never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
RESEND_API_KEY=
MAIL_FROM=
# Who may be emailed, invoices and invitations alike, comma-separated addresses. Anywhere but production
# (TRADER_ENVIRONMENT=production, below) the list is the whole of it: blank, nobody is sent
# to. In production, blank means anyone, except for the Demo door's company (below), which
# is sent to this list alone: blank, it emails nobody.
MAIL_ALLOWLIST=

# The Demo sign-in, read by apps/web/src/server/clerk-demo.ts: the one way in that sends no
# text message, for Apple's beta review and for showing the product. Set together or not at
# all: blank, there is no such door and nobody is let in by it. The code is a secret of 16
# to 128 characters with no space (`openssl rand -base64 24`); whoever has it and the number
# of a person of the company below signs in as that person. The company is the only one the
# door admits, by its id: the Demo company in production, the fixture company on staging.
# Never D'Sierra's. In production that company is closed to the outside, because the code is
# shared: its invoices go only to MAIL_ALLOWLIST and it can invite nobody, so
# invite its people before setting the pair. Staging is not closed.
DEMO_SIGN_IN_CODE=
DEMO_COMPANY_ID=

# Development identity, read by packages/api/src/core/dev-identity.ts and apps/web/src/server/identity.ts.
# It takes Clerk's place: where it is on, nothing of Clerk runs, /sign-in answers 404 and an
# invitation tells no provider. Under NODE_ENV=production it is never consulted, whatever is set.
# Blank is off. `enabled` trusts the x-trader-dev-subject header with x-trader-dev-email,
# x-trader-dev-phone (a +1 E.164 number) or both, or the
# trader-dev-email cookie set by POST /dev-signin (subject `dev:` + the email lowercased), as a
# verified login, and only under NODE_ENV=development or test; under any other NODE_ENV the API
# refuses the request and /dev-signin answers 404. The same while DATABASE_URL is set: a
# deployed database never takes a `dev:` sign-in.
TRADER_DEV_IDENTITY=

# Kill switch, read by packages/api/src/core/status.ts. Server-only, never EXPO_PUBLIC_. Blank is
# normal; `read_only` holds pushes, `paused` holds all sync. Builds below a minimum (a positive
# integer; blank is 1) are told to update. An invalid value answers `paused` and is reported.
# Deployed values change only with a new deployment.
TRADER_SYNC_MODE=
TRADER_MIN_BUILD_IOS=
TRADER_MIN_BUILD_ANDROID=

# Which TRADER environment a deployment is, read by apps/web/src/server/environment.ts:
# `staging` or `production`, nothing else. Blank on a development machine. It is stated and
# never inferred: staging is the staging Vercel project's own Production deployment, so
# Vercel's VERCEL_ENV says `production` there too. It decides the invoice allow-list rule
# above and names the environment on an error report.
TRADER_ENVIRONMENT=

# The host whose `/` is the homepage, where a deployment answers on more than one
# (production: `dsierrapainting.jpteq.app`, D'Sierra's own, beside the neutral
# `app.jpteq.app`). On that host everything else answers as it does anywhere; on any other
# host `/` goes to the office. Blank, as on staging and a development machine, `/` is the
# homepage wherever it is asked for. Read by apps/web/src/server/addresses.ts, which also
# sends a page asked for on a host that is not one of CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES' origins to
# the same path on the first of them.
TRADER_HOME_HOST=

# Where the phone app is got from, for `/get`, the page an invitation points to: the
# TestFlight link and the Play testing link. Public addresses, not secrets. With one blank
# the page says to ask the office instead. Read per request by
# apps/web/src/server/app-links.ts, so a link changes without a build.
TRADER_GET_IOS_URL=
TRADER_GET_ANDROID_URL=

# A deployment (NODE_ENV=production) refuses to start unless TRADER_ENVIRONMENT,
# DATABASE_URL, both Clerk keys, CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES and SENTRY_DSN are set and well
# formed, TRADER_DEV_IDENTITY is blank, the mail pair and the Demo pair are each whole or
# blank, and the three kill-switch variables parse
# (apps/web/src/server/deploy-env.ts). VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA is the platform's own, never
# set by hand: it names the release on a report and the commit `/api/ready` answers.
